WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.740
Before signing a lease, a renter needs
to understand more than the monthly rent.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.340
Blueline Lease highlights consequential
terms and shows the words behind each

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:09.890
flag.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:12.700
Choose the renter perspective,

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.200
then add a selectable-text PDF.

00:00:15.765 --> 00:00:21.575
This local demonstration uses a synthetic
lease and deterministic model responses.

00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:26.147
Read my lease sends
extracted text for review.

00:00:26.362 --> 00:00:28.712
The original file stays on the device.

00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:31.572
Missing required
documents stop the review.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.820
The report ranks flagged
terms by potential harm.

00:00:36.045 --> 00:00:40.535
Here, the lease says remaining rent is
due at once if the renter leaves early.

00:00:40.745 --> 00:00:43.635
The supporting sentence sits
beside that consequence.

00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:48.173
Open the explanation to
see when the risk matters.

00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:53.863
A renter considering a job move now has a
specific term to clarify before signing.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.820
My documented product approach
requires source-backed flags.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:03.765
The server matches each quotation against
the supplied text before the interface

00:01:03.765 --> 00:01:04.895
displays it.

00:01:05.015 --> 00:01:07.925
That verifies the source,
not the interpretation.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.680
The current version reads the agreement.

00:01:11.985 --> 00:01:16.175
It does not check local law or decide
whether a lease is safe to sign.

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:21.930
This build connects a focused renter
workflow with explicit review boundaries

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.760
and citation checks.

00:01:24.025 --> 00:01:27.775
Explore the source and the companion
walkthrough, Inside the Build.

